    "lawCode": "Add §344-r, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7706\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Jake Arcara Worker's Memorial Highway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nDesignates a portion of the state highway system as the \"Jake Acara\nWorker's Memorial Highway\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1- renames part of route 118 in Yorktown, \"Jake Acara Worker's\nMemorial Highway\"\n\nSection 2- The commissioner of transportation shall provide for all\nsignage\n\nSection 3- Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nJake Acara was a highway maintenance worker who was tragically killed on\nthe job by a motorist who sped through the construction zone. This bill\nwould rename part of route 118 in Jake's honor and for all workers who\nare killed while maintaining our roadways.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
